2. FSM STATE SET

2.1 Definition

Definition 1 (FSM State Set M). The agentic FSM has states partitioned into five classes:

```
M = M_task ∪ M_sub ∪ M_halt ∪ M_error ∪ {POWER_DOWN}
```

where:

Class Purpose States
M_task Task-level orchestration IDLE, GOAL_PARSE, PLAN, DECOMPOSE, TASK_COMPLETE
M_sub Sub-task execution SUB_INIT, TRIAGE, SCHEDULE, EXECUTE, VERIFY, COMMIT, NEXT_SUB
M_halt Refusal (bounded, intentional) REFUSE_GOAL, REFUSE_ACT, REFUSE_BUDGET
M_error Failure (invariant violated, timeout) ERROR_TIMEOUT, ERROR_INVARIANT, ERROR_STACK
— Terminal POWER_DOWN

Every state is in s_mode (A4 §2.1). The FSM state set is finite by construction.

