5. CYCLE BUDGET AND T-AET

5.1 Per-State Budget

Each state has a declared cycle cost (the cycle_cost field in the transition rule). The cost is enforced by the hardware cycle counter, same as the base FSM.

State Cost (cycles)
IDLE 0
GOAL_PARSE 60
PLAN 100
DECOMPOSE 80
SUB_INIT 10
TRIAGE 50
SCHEDULE 30
EXECUTE 280
VERIFY 40
COMMIT 40
NEXT_SUB 10
TASK_COMPLETE 20
POWER_DOWN 40

Per-sub-task WCET: SUB_INIT + TRIAGE + SCHEDULE + EXECUTE + VERIFY + COMMIT + NEXT_SUB = 460 cycles.

This is within the base WCET target of 800 ns (460 / 500 MHz = 920 ns — slightly over; the deployment must either reduce EXECUTE or increase clock. This is an A1 design tension noted in §9).

5.2 Task-Level AET (T-AET)

Definition 4 (T-AET). The task-level Assured Execution Time is the maximum number of cycles the entire task may consume:

```
T-AET = C_task_overhead + (N_max × C_subtask)
```

where:

· C_task_overhead = GOAL_PARSE + PLAN + DECOMPOSE + TASK_COMPLETE + POWER_DOWN = 300 cycles
· N_max = maximum sub-tasks per task = K × D_invoke (A3 §4)
· C_subtask = 460 cycles

For K = 64, D_invoke = 3: T-AET = 300 + 192 × 460 = 88,620 cycles ≈ 177 µs.

At 500 MHz, this is well within task-level budget budget_max = 10⁶ cycles (A3 §4).

5.3 Budget Enforcement

At every transition, the cycle counter is incremented. If the counter exceeds T-AET:

· Transition to REFUSE_BUDGET.
· Log 0x-BUDGET-EXCEEDED.
· Halt.

The FSM does not run forever. It cannot. The bound is structural.

---

6. THE SUB-TASK LOOP

6.1 Sub-Task Queue

DECOMPOSE produces a queue of sub-tasks (A3 §6). The FSM consumes the queue one sub-task at a time via the loop:

```
SUB_INIT → TRIAGE → SCHEDULE → EXECUTE → VERIFY → COMMIT → NEXT_SUB → SUB_INIT
```

6.2 Sub-Task State

Each sub-task has an entry in s_ctx.current:

```
sub_task = ⟨ sub_id, action_or_plan, params, status, attempt ⟩
```

status ∈ {PENDING, RUNNING, VERIFIED, COMMITTED, REFUSED, RETRIED}.

attempt is the retry counter (A3 §7.2). Bounded by the plan's declared retry policy.

6.3 Sub-Task Termination

A sub-task terminates in exactly one of:

Outcome Transition
COMMIT succeeded NEXT_SUB
VERIFY failed, policy = Halt REFUSE_ACT
VERIFY failed, policy = Retry TRIAGE (attempt++)
VERIFY failed, policy = Rollback restore checkpoint → TRIAGE
Timeout ERROR_TIMEOUT
Invariant violated ERROR_INVARIANT

Every path is finite. Every path is logged.

