APPENDIX A — Plain Language

What is a state machine?
A rulebook that says: if you're here, and this happens, go there.
What is the FSM's job in the agent?
To walk the agent through every step of every task, one state at a time, in a bounded way.
What does "bounded" mean?
It means the FSM cannot run forever. It has a budget. When the budget is spent, it stops.
What happens if a step fails?
The FSM has three exits: refuse, error, or continue. All of them are named. All of them are logged.
Can the FSM ever do something unexpected?
No. Every state has declared transitions. Every transition has a declared cost. There are no surprise states.
What is this called?
A1 — the FSM extension.

